  "tracks": {
    "single": {
      "label": "Readings",
      "readings": [
        {
          "role": "first",
          "ref": "Acts 1:15-17, 21-26",
          "refKey": "Acts.1.15-Acts.1.17",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "call-and-discipleship",
              "mission-and-witness",
              "providence-and-care"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "resolve-and-sending"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 15,
              "v_end": 15,
              "text": "The number of persons together — Who were together in the upper room. were a hundred and twenty - But he had undoubtedly many more in other places; of whom more than five hundred saw him at once after his resurrection, 1 Cor. xv, 6."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 16,
              "v_end": 16,
              "text": "Psalm xli, 9."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "psalm",
          "ref": "Psalm 1",
          "refKey": "Ps.1",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faithfulness",
              "justice"
            ],
            "image": [
              "road-and-journey",
              "water"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "trust"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "Blessed — The Hebrew words are very emphatical: O the blessedness of that man! Counsel - That doth not lead his life according to their counsel, or manner of living. Standeth - Which notes a more settled abode in it. Way - In their manner of conversation. Seat - Which notes a constant and resolved perseverance in their wicked courses. Scornful - Of those who make a mock of sin, and scoff at goodness and goodmen. Divers observe a gradation in this verse; the following clause still exceeding the former, for standing is more than walking, and sitting more than standing; and sinners in scripture use, are worse than the ungodly, and the scornful are the worst of sinners."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Day and night — Not seldom and slightly, but diligently, and constantly."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "Whither — His happiness is not short and transitory, but, like those trees which are continually green and flourishing."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "Ungodly — Their condition is far different. Chaff - They are restless and unquiet: their seeming felicity, hath no firm foundation, but quickly vanishes and flees away as chaff before the wind."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "Not stand — Not endure the trial. Judgment - In the great and general judgment of the world."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "Knoweth — He approves, loves, and delights in them, and therefore will recompence them. Perish - All their designs and courses shall come to nothing, and they shall perish with them. There is nothing in this psalm which is not applicable to Christ, but some things which are not all applicable to David. Threatenings denounced against the adversaries of Christ's kingdom, ver. 1-6. Promises made to Christ, ver. 7-9. Counsel given to all, to submit to him, ver. 10-12."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "1 John 5:9-13",
          "refKey": "1John.5.9-1John.5.13",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faith-and-trust",
              "resurrection-and-life",
              "word-of-god"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "assurance"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "If we receive the testimony of men — As we do continually, and must do in a thousand instances. The testimony of God is greater - Of higher authority, and much more worthy to be received; namely, this very testimony which God the Father, together with the Word and the Spirit, hath testified of the Son, as the saviour of the world."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "He that believeth on the Son of God hath the testimony — The dear evidence of this, in himself: he that believeth not God, in this, hath made him a liar; because he supposes that to be false which God has expressly testified."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "And this is the sum of that testimony, that God hath given us a title to, and the real beginning of, eternal life; and that this is purchased by, and treasured up in, his Son, who has all the springs and the fulness of it in himself, to communicate to his body, the church, first in grace and then in glory."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 12,
              "v_end": 12,
              "text": "It plainly follows, he that hath the Son — Living and reigning in him by faith. Hath this life; he that hath not the Son of God hath not this life - Hath no part or lot therein. In the former clause, the apostle says simply, the Son; because believers know him: in the latter, the Son of God; that unbelievers may know how great a blessing they fall short of."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 13,
              "v_end": 13,
              "text": "These things have I written — In the introduction, chap. i, 4, he said, I write: now, in the close, I have written. That ye may know - With a fuller and stronger assurance, that ye have eternal life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "gospel",
          "ref": "John 17:6-19",
          "refKey": "John.17.6-John.17.19",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "church-and-unity",
              "mission-and-witness",
              "prayer-and-worship",
              "word-of-god"
            ],
            "image": [
              "name"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "longing-and-waiting",
              "tenderness"
            ],
            "function": [
              "lament-intercession"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "I have manifested thy name — All thy attributes; and in particular thy paternal relation to believers; to the men whom thou hast given me - The apostles, and so ver. 12. They were thine - By creation, and by descent from Abraham. And thou hast given them me - By giving them faith in what I have spoken. So ver. 9."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 7,
              "v_end": 7,
              "text": "Now they know that all things — Which I have done and spoken, are of thee - And consequently right and true."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "They have received them — By faith."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "I pray not for the world — Not in these petitions, which are adapted to the state of believers only. (He prays for the world at ver. 21, 23, that they may believe - That they may know God hath sent him.) This no more proves that our Lord did not pray for the world, both before and afterward, than his praying for the apostles alone, ver. 6-19, proves that he did not pray for them also which shall believe through their word, ver. 20."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "All things that are mine are thine, and that are thine are mine — These are very high and strong expressions, too grand for any mere creature to use; as implying that all things whatsoever, inclusive of the Divine nature, perfections, and operations, are the common property of the Father and the Son. And this is the original ground of that peculiar property, which both the Father and the Son have in the persons who were given to Christ as Mediator; according to what is said in the close of the verse, of his being glorified by them; namely, believing in him, and so acknowledging his glory."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "Keep them through thy name — Thy power, mercy, wisdom, that they may be one - with us and with each other; one body, separate from the world: as we are - By resemblance to us, though not equality."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 12,
              "v_end": 12,
              "text": "Those whom thou hast given me I have guarded, and none of them is lost, but the son of perdition — So one even of them whom God had given him is lost. So far was even that decree from being unchangeable! That the Scripture might be fulfilled - That is, whereby the Scripture was fulfilled. The son of perdition signifies one that deservedly perishes; as a son of death, 2 Sam. xii, 5; children of hell, Matt. xxiii, 15, and children of wrath, Eph. ii, 3, signify persons justly obnoxious to death, hell, wrath. Psalm cix, 8."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 13,
              "v_end": 13,
              "text": "In the world — That is, before I leave the world. My joy - The joy I feel at going to the Father."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 15,
              "v_end": 15,
              "text": "That thou wouldest take them out of the world — Not yet: but that thou wouldest keep them from the evil one - Who reigns therein."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 17,
              "v_end": 17,
              "text": "Sanctify — Consecrate them by the anointing of thy Spirit to their office, and perfect them in holiness, by means of thy word."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 17,
              "v_start": 19,
              "v_end": 19,
              "text": "I sanctify myself — I devote myself as a victim, to be sacrificed."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
